like, a charming look to it and was pretty cool.

00:43:35.670 --> 00:43:39.810
I think the controls keep it off of the Essential Games list.

00:43:41.250 --> 00:43:47.990
Specifically, the weird registering of the hitboxes and me not really knowing when I'm

00:43:47.990 --> 00:43:48.930
going to hit, when I'm not.

00:43:49.330 --> 00:43:51.070
Sometimes it feels like I should have hit and I didn't.

00:43:52.290 --> 00:43:53.350
That keeps it out.

00:43:53.450 --> 00:43:58.550
But I think it was better than a lot of these games that try and do, like, wrestling or karate

00:43:58.550 --> 00:43:59.690
that we've played in the past.

00:44:00.270 --> 00:44:01.750
Not all of them, but some of them.

00:44:02.370 --> 00:44:03.390
All right. Sean?

00:44:04.130 --> 00:44:13.810
So, this game, for me, it's interesting that you can see the primordial ooze of the beat-em-up.

00:44:14.890 --> 00:44:17.370
But it's really blurry.

00:44:17.890 --> 00:44:26.750
This is the most far away from it with while still being a beat-em-up that can possibly exist.

00:44:28.130 --> 00:44:30.530
The polish isn't there.

00:44:33.030 --> 00:44:39.810
The backgrounds are nice for the NES, but everything else is just sort of messy.

00:44:40.050 --> 00:44:43.270
It's got bad handwriting all over it, so it's not essential.

00:44:43.930 --> 00:44:45.190
Got it. All right.

00:44:45.330 --> 00:44:47.490
And I also have a straight thought that I just remembered.

00:44:47.490 --> 00:44:53.170
I want to talk about, since we joked about power-ups, like, if you needed a shoulder throw

00:44:53.170 --> 00:45:01.570
power-up, but there is a power-up called power-up, which turns you into one-punch man, where it's

00:45:01.570 --> 00:45:05.250
described in a manual as a power P will appear.

00:45:05.470 --> 00:45:10.650
If the renegade can catch it, he will be able to knock down his enemies with one punch and

00:45:10.650 --> 00:45:11.470
can do so.

00:45:11.610 --> 00:45:12.590
And so, I just thought that was kind of fun.

00:45:12.590 --> 00:45:13.790
And they go flying off the screen.

00:45:13.950 --> 00:45:17.270
It's cool. Yeah. I think that's, like, neat as, like, a bonus thing.

00:45:17.370 --> 00:45:21.190
But it only shows up depending on the last two digits of the timer.

00:45:21.330 --> 00:45:22.990
Yeah. It's really weird. And that's very strange.

00:45:23.050 --> 00:45:24.710
And you have to kick something at those last two digits.

00:45:24.790 --> 00:45:26.230
You have to, like, time your kick.

00:45:26.270 --> 00:45:27.630
Yeah. You have to jump kick the enemy.

00:45:27.830 --> 00:45:29.530
Right. Yeah. It's ridiculous.

00:45:29.810 --> 00:45:34.770
But what's funny is that they say in the manual, hint, jump kick the enemy when the last two

00:45:34.770 --> 00:45:36.310
digits of the timer are as follows.

00:45:36.490 --> 00:45:37.390
That's not a hint.

00:45:37.410 --> 00:45:38.270
That's a rule. Yeah.

00:45:38.310 --> 00:45:39.370
That's a good answer. Yeah.

00:45:39.370 --> 00:45:44.190
That's, like, please note the only way, like, it's weird.

00:45:44.350 --> 00:45:46.750
You know, it's almost like the hint should have just been the first part.

00:45:46.770 --> 00:45:49.750
And then it's, like, you figure out what time it has to be.

00:45:49.830 --> 00:45:50.890
But they didn't care.

00:45:51.050 --> 00:45:52.110
That would be a pain, too, though.

00:45:52.390 --> 00:45:54.010
Yeah. I will say this.

00:45:54.250 --> 00:45:55.430
Weird thought on this one.

00:45:55.770 --> 00:46:02.970
If it was 1988 and we were, like, the current, like, news people for video games and we were

00:46:02.970 --> 00:46:07.570
recommending things, I would recommend this game right now, like, because it's just,

00:46:07.670 --> 00:46:09.270
like, hey, you should have this in your collection.

00:46:09.750 --> 00:46:12.010
NES fans. If it was 1988.

00:46:12.550 --> 00:46:16.690
I think this game is doing, like, you know, something so different from what we've been

00:46:16.690 --> 00:46:18.190
offered in the catalog so far.

00:46:18.930 --> 00:46:23.210
But I'm not going to say in 2019 here that it's worth it.

00:46:23.450 --> 00:46:31.170
It's not worth it on any scale, really, because of how bizarre the controller layout is for dealing

00:46:31.170 --> 00:46:35.690
with enemies. And then on top of that, I also don't think that, like, you know, how Sean was talking

00:46:35.690 --> 00:46:38.430
about, this is just the first bearings of a beat-em-up.

00:46:38.430 --> 00:46:41.070
I don't think the whole picture has been figured out yet.

00:46:41.290 --> 00:46:44.610
I think this leaves me kind of excited for Target Renegade.

00:46:44.990 --> 00:46:48.650
You know, like, I'm not saying, like, oh, Renegade was pretty bad, so I'm not looking

00:46:48.650 --> 00:46:50.730
forward to this 1990 sequel.

00:46:50.730 --> 00:46:55.170
I'm looking forward to seeing if they learn anything, if the, when Taito makes the game,

00:46:55.390 --> 00:46:56.910
if they take any lessons from it.

00:46:57.630 --> 00:47:02.370
But it's just weird to say that, like, had it have been 1988, I could have totally seen

00:47:02.370 --> 00:47:05.310
myself being like, yeah, everyone should have a copy of this.

00:47:05.430 --> 00:47:07.170
Like, this is something that we haven't seen yet.

00:47:07.330 --> 00:47:08.170
Like, go for it.

00:47:08.890 --> 00:47:11.370
But today, I won't even recommend it.

00:47:11.370 --> 00:47:12.310
I'm trying to think.

00:47:12.470 --> 00:47:17.130
I'm trying to think if I would have, if this was the only exposure to the genre that I had,

00:47:17.150 --> 00:47:18.750
if I would have said the same.

00:47:18.890 --> 00:47:24.510
And I think that without the knowledge that this, without the knowledge of what these games

00:47:25.330 --> 00:47:30.470
are and were, so that I sort of had a basic understanding of how they operated, I don't

00:47:30.470 --> 00:47:31.950
know if I would have liked it that much.

00:47:32.110 --> 00:47:33.330
I don't know. Got it.

00:47:33.530 --> 00:47:37.130
I think that there is enough, like, charisma in this game.

00:47:37.310 --> 00:47:41.410
Sure. That makes me also, like, there's like a charm factor to it, too.

00:47:41.930 --> 00:47:47.370
That, and the fact that you can skip between the first three stages, like, so this way

00:47:47.370 --> 00:47:49.330
you don't have to actually be good at the game.

00:47:49.410 --> 00:47:50.470
You can still experience it.

00:47:50.730 --> 00:47:52.930
All those things are, like, thumbs up in my book.

